# chmod Command (Change Mode)

`chmod` is used to change the permissions of files and directories.

Permissions control who can read, write, or execute a file.

---

## Permission Values

| Permission | Symbol | Number |
|-----------|--------|--------|
| read      | `r`    | 4      |
| write     | `w`    | 2      |
| execute   | `x`    | 1      |

---

## Permission Groups

| Group | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `u`  | user (owner) |
| `g`  | group |
| `o`  | others |
| `a`  | all |

---

## chmod Symbols

| Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| `+` | add permission |
| `-` | remove permission |
| `=` | set exact permission |

### Examples

| Command | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| `chmod u+x file` | add execute permission to user |
| `chmod g-w file` | remove write permission from group |
| `chmod o=r file` | set others permission to read only |

